==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*ľudьje||people, men}}, from {{inh|sh|ine-bsl-pro|*ljaudis||people, men}} from {{etyl|ine-pro|sh}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sh|/ʎûːdi/}}
* {{hyphenation|sh|lju|di}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m-p|head=ljȗdi}}; singular: {{l|sh|čȍvjek}} / {{l|sh|čȍvek}})

# [[people]], [[men]]
#: {{ux|sh|Dva ''čovjeka'' su išla cestom|Two '''men''' walked down the street.}}
#: {{ux|sh|Pet ''ljudi'' je išlo cestom.|Five '''people''' walked down the street.}}
# {{lb|sh|colloquial}} [[guys]], [[you guys]] (group of familiar people of any or mixed gender)
# {{lb|sh|vocative}} [[everybody]], [[everyone]] (addressing a group of people)

====Usage notes====
This plural form takes suppletive stem in the singular, as can be seen in the declension table. Old dual forms have been preserved in the counting for 2, 3, 4 (also for 22, 23, 24, 32, 33, 34, etc., whereas the singular form is used for 21, 31, 41, etc.) which bind plural form of {{m|sh|čȍvjek}} / {{m|sh|čȍvek}}.

